    "title": "Shakespeare's Spooktacular Halloween Party | NewsBreak",
    "text": "Shakespeare's Spooktacular Halloween Party\nBy the pricking of my thumbs, something wicked this way comes!\nGet Ticket\nDate and time\n- Oct 24, 2025 08:00 PM - 11:00 PM\nLocation\nThe Robert Toombs House, 216 East Robert Toombs Avenue, Washington, GA 30673About this event\nShakespeare's Spooktacular Halloween Party\nOn Friday, October 24th, the boundaries between reality and fantasy fade away.\nJoin us and step into a domain where love and tragedy intertwine, and where Shakespeare’s dark truths echo softly through the hush of the night.\nThroughout the night, readings from Macbeth, Hamlet, Titus Andronicus, and other cursed tales of the Bard will be performed by brave partygoers who have volunteered to become part of the magic—though participation is entirely optional.\nIf inspiration strikes, Shakespeare’s own favorite passages will be laid out, ready for those who wish to read and summon the spirits of the stage.\nGuests are encouraged to wear their most magical costumes and enchanting attire—to fully immerse themselves in the mystical world. Mortal garb is also welcome for those who prefer a subtler touch.\nWhile under the enchantment, enjoy some tasty treats and be sure to indulge in some of the sinister \"poisoned\" punch to help satisfy your thirst for the macabre.",
